"""Triton implementation of ``aten::_cast_Half``: elementwise narrowing cast to float16.

Native semantics reproduced here:

* every element is converted with round-to-nearest-even to IEEE binary16,
  subnormals included, and out-of-range magnitudes become +/-Inf;
* ``float64`` sources are rounded *through* float32 first (the native
  constructor takes a ``float``), which is observably different from a direct
  64->16 cast near fp16 rounding ties;
* complex sources keep only the real component;
* a ``float16`` source is returned as the very same object (native identity);
* an empty source returns an allocated empty float16 tensor without a launch;
* the backward pass converts the upstream float16 gradient back to the input
  dtype, exposed through a differentiable forward so autograd can reach it.

Conversions run entirely in Triton kernels. Shape and stride metadata is passed
as compile-time constants and complex real components are read in the kernel.
Output allocation still needs a tensor allocator.
"""

